
# FLY
### Drone Flight Simulation & Autonomous Systems

FLY is an open-source drone simulation project built to explore the engineering behind unmanned aerial systems (UAS), flight dynamics, and autonomous navigation.

The goal is simple: **understand how drones work by building a simulator from the ground up.**

Inspired by modern aerospace and defense technology, FLY aims to combine realistic flight physics, interactive controls, and autonomous navigation in a single simulation environment.

## Overview

FLY is an experimental platform for learning and developing:

- **Flight Dynamics** — Thrust, gravity, drag, torque, and stability.
- **Flight Control** — Manual piloting, attitude control, and PID stabilization.
- **Autonomous Navigation** — Waypoint following, path planning, and obstacle avoidance.
- **Sensor Simulation** — IMU, GPS, altitude, and simulated camera inputs.
- **Mission Planning** — Interactive environments, flight paths, and telemetry.

## Development Roadmap

### Phase 01 — Flight
- [ ] Build a 3D simulation environment
- [ ] Create a controllable quadcopter
- [ ] Implement basic flight physics
- [ ] Add keyboard and mouse controls
- [ ] Display real-time flight telemetry

### Phase 02 — Control
- [ ] Implement PID flight controllers
- [ ] Simulate motor thrust and torque
- [ ] Add altitude and position hold
- [ ] Model wind and environmental disturbances

### Phase 03 — Autonomy
- [ ] Implement waypoint navigation
- [ ] Develop autonomous takeoff and landing
- [ ] Introduce obstacle detection and avoidance
- [ ] Build a mission-planning interface

### Phase 04 — Simulation
- [ ] Create multiple 3D environments
- [ ] Simulate onboard sensors
- [ ] Add flight recording and replay
- [ ] Compare manual and autonomous performance

## Technical Architecture

The planned simulation consists of four systems:

1. **Physics Engine** — Models the drone's motion and forces.
2. **Flight Controller** — Converts control inputs into motor commands.
3. **Autonomy Engine** — Handles navigation and mission execution.
4. **Visualization Layer** — Renders the environment, drone, and telemetry.

## Project Philosophy

Build to understand.

Rather than treating drone flight as a black box, FLY is designed to make the underlying engineering visible, interactive, and understandable.

Every system is an opportunity to learn how real autonomous aircraft operate.

